+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+The `muninn-bench perf` full-recall case uses the adversarial synthetic store whose
+frequent vocabulary is the 30 words in `crates/muninn-bench/src/main.rs`. With the
+benchmark defaults (5,000 records, 15,000 cues, and 300 hook invocations), the
+`UserPromptSubmit` full-recall p95 was **11.458564 ms** before the term-selection
+fix.
+
+The fix was to discard a candidate prompt term when its document frequency is
+greater than one third of a store containing at least 50 active records, before
+sorting the remaining candidates by IDF and taking the top eight. This prevents
+low-signal terms from forcing FTS5 to traverse the synthetic vocabulary's long
+posting lists.
+
+With that fix in place, the same benchmark measured a full-recall p95 of
+**1.565942 ms**.
